{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310816,"nonce":"ovFRRFo9ENJ8Fdx8TxVOGikE4QM=","title":"Host-parallel Q8 flash attention for wasm decode — landed, +5%→+13% scaling win; the lingering-process benchmark hazard that nearly buried ...","message":"Host-parallel Q8_0 flash attention for the `rayzor run --wasm` decode path. The\nwasm guest computes attention SERIALLY while the host worker pool (the same one\nhost_parallel_qmatmul uses) spins idle. This seam bands `num_kv_heads` across\nthat idle native pool. Validated and lint-clean; NOT yet committed (was on main).\n\n**Seam (6 files, +417 LOC):**\n- `compiler/src/codegen/wasm_runner.rs`: `host_parallel_flash_q8()` (kernel,\n  copies the serial nue-plugins compute VERBATIM — NEON dq/dotb/axpyb + per-band\n  `vec![]` scratch, safe on real-TLS host threads; `libm::expf` softmax to match\n  the wasm guest's `fmath::exp` = libm::expf bit-for-bit) + host-import\n  registration `rayzor_host_flash_attn_q8_par` (12 i32 params; reconstruct scale\n  via `f32::from_bits`; base via `caller.data().shared_memory`). Gated off by\n  `RAYZOR_WASM_NO_HOST_MATMUL=1` OR new `RAYZOR_WASM_NO_HOST_FLASH=1` (isolates\n  the attention A/B while keeping host matmul on).\n- `runtime-wasm/src/qtensor.rs`: dispatcher `rayzor_tensor_flash_attn_q8_host`\n  (reads KvCacheQ8Hdr {data,max_seq_len,num_kv_heads,head_dim,head_dim_bytes} +\n  Q tensor, validates contiguity, allocs `[1,nqh,hd]` output, calls the host\n  import; on 0 frees output + returns 0 → caller falls back). Lives in the MAIN\n  module, resolved by the normal export-merge (NOT a Q8 side-module trampoline).\n- `nue-plugins/src/lib.rs`: NativeMethodDesc row `flashAttnDecodeQ8Host` →\n  `rayzor_tensor_flash_attn_q8_host` `[Ptr,Ptr,Ptr,I64,I64,F64]=\u003ePtr` +\n  plugin_init entry + native stub returning 0 (`#[cfg(not(wasm32))]` — native\n  always falls back to serial; gated off wasm so the side-module never shadows\n  the main-module dispatcher).\n- `nue/transformer/KvCacheQ8.hx` extern method; `GQAttention.hx` try-host-then-\n  `flashAttnDecodeQ8` fallback.\n\n**CRITICAL ABI fact:** `ir_type_to_wasm` maps EVERYTHING except F32/F64/Vector\n→ wasm **i32** (so IrType::I64 → i32, not i64!). The desc `[...,I64,I64,F64]=\u003ePtr`\nlowers to guest import `(i32,i32,i32,i32,i32,f64)-\u003ei32`. The main-module\ndispatcher must match that EXACTLY or the linker stubs it to return-0 (silent\nfallback, no crash). The Q8 SIDE-MODULE path needs a trampoline (coerce_val)\nbecause the side-module's Rust i64 sig differs; the merged main-module path does\nNOT. See [[perf_wasm_host_parallel_matmul]].\n\n**Results (M1 Pro, Llama-3.2-1B Q4_K_M, RAYZOR_KV_Q8=1, --no-cache, greedy):**\n- cache_len ~235 (200 tok): p50 78.5 vs 83 ms = **+5%**, reproducible 2 pairs.\n- cache_len ~635 (600 tok): p50 79.5 vs 88 = **+10%**, p95 ~84 vs 96 = **+13%**,\n  wall ~48.8 vs 53.3 = +8.5%. Win SCALES with context (attention is a bigger\n  fwd-pass fraction at long ctx). ON#1==ON#2 p50 → deterministic. France→\"Paris\"\n  byte-identical ON vs OFF. No cache_len gate needed (host pool already warm from\n  matmul, so dispatch is cheap; wins even at the short-step-inclusive p50).\n\nWhy this lever worked when the IN-GUEST q-head flash parallelization was reverted\n(see [[bugs_wasm_oom_and_object_freeing]]): host threads have real TLS + don't\ntouch guest malloc; each kv_head band reads shared K/V/Q read-only and writes a\nDISJOINT output band — same safety property as the proven host matmul pool.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `perf_wasm_host_parallel_flash_q8` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}